### \`tls.d.progress-ring\` — Progress Ring

Ring filled to value / max with the figure in the centre, plus label and caption. _(family: data; keywords: progress, ring, dial, percent, completion, score)_

**When:** One completion rate or score shown as a dial.
**Avoid:** Shares of several parts (use tls.d.donut); several bars (use tls.d.progress-bar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | yes | number | Ring fills to value / max. |
| \`max\` | no | number | Value that fills the ring. Default 100. |
| \`label\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | What it measures. |
| \`caption\` | no | text (max 80 chars) | One line of context. |
| \`thickness\` | no | enum: md \\\\| sm \\\\| lg |  |
| \`cap\` | no | enum: round \\\\| flat |  |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| status | status = red/amber/green by progress. |
| \`format\` | no | enum: percent \\\\| plain \\\\| compact \\\\| currency | percent = share of max. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_ring\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.progress-ring\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": 68,
    \\"label\\": \\"Course completion\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"34 of 50 lessons\\",
    \\"tone\\": \\"status\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.radar\` — Radar Chart

Spider chart: up to three shapes over three to eight axes, with grid rings and values. _(family: data; keywords: radar, spider, profile, skills, scores, criteria)_

**When:** Profiles on several criteria (skills, product scores).
**Avoid:** More than 3 series or 8 axes (use tls.d.compare-table); exact values (use tls.d.grouped-bar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`axes\` | yes | list of text (max 24 chars) (3–8 items) | Criteria around the dial, in order. |
| \`series\` | yes | list of object (name, values) (1–3 items) | One shape each; one value per axis. |
| \`max\` | no | number | Default: the largest value, rounded up. |
| \`fill\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`rings\` | no | number | Grid rings, 1-8. Default 4. |
| \`legend\` | no | enum: top \\\\| bottom \\\\| right \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_radar\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.radar\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"axes\\": [
      \\"Speed\\",
      \\"Cost\\",
      \\"Quality\\",
      \\"Support\\"
    ],
    \\"series\\": [
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Ours\\",
        \\"values\\": [
          8,
          6,
          9,
          7
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.d.ranking\` — Ranking

Leaderboard rows: position, name, value bar and value, with medals for the top three. _(family: data; keywords: ranking, leaderboard, top 10, top n, best, league table)_

**When:** Top-N lists, leaderboards, top products.
**Avoid:** No ranking intent (tls.d.bar). Many columns: tls.d.table.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (label, value, note) (3–10 items) | Any order: sorted by value unless sort is none. |
| \`showBars\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`medals\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`sort\` | no | enum: desc \\\\| asc \\\\| none |  |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_ranking\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.ranking\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Aurora\\",
