### \`tls.g.matrix-2x2\` — 2x2 Matrix

Two-by-two quadrant grid with labelled axes and optional plotted points. _(family: diagram; keywords: matrix, 2x2, quadrant, prioritisation)_

**When:** Contrast on two dimensions: effort/impact, urgent/important, BCG.
**Avoid:** Many numeric points (use tls.d.scatter); SWOT (use tls.g.swot).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`xAxis\` | yes | object (low, high, title) | {low, high, title?} of the horizontal dimension. |
| \`yAxis\` | yes | object (low, high, title) | {low, high, title?}; high is at the top. |
| \`quadrants\` | yes | list of object (label, text) (4–4 items) | Exactly 4 {label, text?}: TL, TR, BL, BR. |
| \`items\` | no | list of object (label, x, y) (0–12 items) | Points {label, x, y}, x and y in 0..1. |
| \`highlight\` | no | enum: none \\\\| TL \\\\| TR \\\\| BL \\\\| BR |  |
| \`style\` | no | enum: tinted \\\\| lines |  |
| \`showItems\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showAxisTitles\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_matrix\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.matrix-2x2\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"xAxis\\": {
      \\"low\\": \\"Low\\",
      \\"high\\": \\"High\\",
      \\"title\\": \\"Effort\\"
    },
    \\"yAxis\\": {
      \\"low\\": \\"Low\\",
      \\"high\\": \\"High\\",
      \\"title\\": \\"Impact\\"
    },
    \\"quadrants\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Quick wins\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Big bets\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Fill-ins\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Avoid\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Onboarding\\",
        \\"x\\": 0.2,
        \\"y\\": 0.8
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.milestones\` — Milestones

Key checkpoints as diamonds on a line, filled when done, each with a date and short label. _(family: diagram; keywords: milestones, checkpoints, dates, progress, deadlines)_

**When:** Dated order of key checkpoints only (no descriptions).
**Avoid:** Events that need descriptions (use tls.g.timeline).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (date, label, done) (2–8 items) | Checkpoints in date order; no descriptions. |
| \`axis\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| vertical |  |
| \`labels\` | no | enum: alternate \\\\| below | alternate = date and label swap sides; below = date above, label below. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_milestones\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.milestones\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"Jan\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Kick-off\\",
        \\"done\\": true
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"Mar\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Prototype\\",
        \\"done\\": true
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"Jun\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Beta release\\"
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"Sep\\",
        \\"label\\": \\"Launch\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.pyramid\` — Pyramid

Stacked pyramid levels from tip to base, each with a label and a note; can be inverted. _(family: diagram; keywords: pyramid, levels, tiers, maslow, hierarchy of needs, foundation)_

**When:** Level: ranked tiers that build on each other, such as Maslow, priority tiers or foundation-to-goal stacks.
**Avoid:** Equal-weight layers (use tls.g.layers) or a narrowing process (use tls.g.funnel).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`levels\` | yes | list of object (label, text) (3–6 items) | Top (tip) first, base last. Keep the tip label short. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: up \\\\| down | down = inverted pyramid, widest level first. |
| \`notes\` | no | enum: side \\\\| inside \\\\| none | side = notes beside the pyramid with leaders. |
| \`fill\` | no | enum: gradient \\\\| series \\\\| single |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_pyramid\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.pyramid\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"levels\\": [
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Purpose\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Why we exist\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Strategy\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Where we play\\"
      },
      {
        \\"label\\": \\"Operations\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"How we deliver every day\\"
      }
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.roadmap\` — Roadmap

Lanes of bars across periods, coloured by status, with a today line. _(family: diagram; keywords: roadmap, gantt, plan, schedule, lanes, quarters)_

**When:** Dated order with overlap: product roadmap, project plan, semester plan.
**Avoid:** Single-point events (use tls.g.timeline or tls.g.milestones).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`periods\` | yes | list of text (max 12 chars) (2–12 items) | Column headers in time order: Q1..Q4, months. |
| \`lanes\` | yes | list of object (name, items) (1–6 items) | Per lane: name, items[{label,start,end,status done\\\\|active\\\\|planned\\\\|risk}]; start/end = 0-based period index, end inclusive. |
| \`todayAt\` | no | number (min -1, max 12) | Period index, fractions ok (1.5 = mid second period); -1 none. |
| \`statusColors\` | no | boolean | Off = one colour per lane. |
| \`laneLabels\` | no | enum: left \\\\| none |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_roadmap\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.roadmap\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"periods\\": [
      \\"Q1\\",
      \\"Q2\\",
      \\"Q3\\",
      \\"Q4\\"
    ],
    \\"lanes\\": [
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Product\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          {
            \\"label\\": \\"Redesign\\",
            \\"start\\": 0,
            \\"end\\": 1,
            \\"status\\": \\"done\\"
          },
          {
            \\"label\\": \\"Mobile app\\",
            \\"start\\": 1.5,
            \\"end\\": 3,
            \\"status\\": \\"active\\"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        \\"name\\": \\"Platform\\",
        \\"items\\": [
          {
            \\"label\\": \\"Migration\\",
            \\"start\\": 0.5,
            \\"end\\": 2,
            \\"status\\": \\"active\\"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    \\"todayAt\\": 1.5
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.steps\` — Steps Diagram

Numbered process diagram with animated step reveal. _(family: diagram; keywords: steps, process, workflow, diagram, flow)_

**When:** Use to illustrate a multi-step process or workflow.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a full process slide with a description per step (use tls.c.steps), or for a single concept (use tls.m.icon-label).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`steps\` | no | text (max 2000 chars) | Array of step objects with title and description. Parsed from JSON array. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| vertical | Layout direction for steps. |
| \`connector\` | no | enum: line \\\\| arrow \\\\| none | Type of connector between steps. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_steps_1\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.steps\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"steps\\": [
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Setup\\",
        \\"description\\": \\"Initialize the environment\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Configure\\",
        \\"description\\": \\"Set up your preferences\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Run\\",
        \\"description\\": \\"Execute the main process\\"
      },
      {
        \\"title\\": \\"Review\\",
        \\"description\\": \\"Verify the results\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"direction\\": \\"horizontal\\",
    \\"connector\\": \\"line\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.swot\` — SWOT

SWOT grid: strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats as four bullet lists. _(family: diagram; keywords: swot, strengths, weaknesses, opportunities, threats, assessment)_

**When:** Contrast: a strategic assessment of an organisation, product or idea (internal vs external, good vs bad).
**Avoid:** Any other two-axis grid (use tls.g.matrix-2x2) or a plain pro/con list (use tls.g.pros-cons).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`strengths\` | yes | list of text (max 80 chars) (1–5 items) | Internal positives, 3-5 short phrases. |
| \`weaknesses\` | yes | list of text (max 80 chars) (1–5 items) | Internal negatives. |
| \`opportunities\` | yes | list of text (max 80 chars) (1–5 items) | External positives. |
| \`threats\` | yes | list of text (max 80 chars) (1–5 items) | External negatives. |
| \`style\` | no | enum: tinted \\\\| outline | tinted = coloured cards, outline = neutral cards. |
| \`letters\` | no | boolean | A large S, W, O or T above each heading. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_swot\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.swot\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"strengths\\": [
      \\"Strong brand\\",
      \\"Loyal users\\"
    ],
    \\"weaknesses\\": [
      \\"Small budget\\"
    ],
    \\"opportunities\\": [
      \\"New markets\\"
    ],
    \\"threats\\": [
      \\"New entrants\\"
    ]
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.timeline\` — Timeline

Dated events along a horizontal or vertical axis, with a card per event and an optional now marker. _(family: diagram; keywords: timeline, history, dates, schedule, milestones, chronology)_

**When:** Dated order: history, project timeline, course schedule.
**Avoid:** Undated steps (use tls.g.steps). Overlapping periods go in tls.g.roadmap.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`events\` | yes | list of object (date, title, text, icon) (3–8 items) | Events in date order, earliest first. |
| \`axis\` | no | enum: horizontal \\\\| vertical |  |
| \`alternate\` | no | boolean | Cards alternate above/below (or left/right) so more events fit. |
| \`nowIndex\` | no | number (min -1, max 20) | 0-based index of the latest event reached; later events are muted. -1 for none. |
| \`nodeStyle\` | no | enum: dot \\\\| icon \\\\| number |  |
| \`showText\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_timeline\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.timeline\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"events\\": [
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"2021\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Founded\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Two founders and a prototype\\"
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"2022\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"First customers\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Ten pilots go live\\"
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"2023\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Series A\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Team grows to thirty\\"
      },
      {
        \\"date\\": \\"2024\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Global launch\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Available in twelve countries\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"nowIndex\\": 2
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.g.tree\` — Tree

Org chart or hierarchy: a root box linked to children and grandchildren, top-down or left to right. _(family: diagram; keywords: tree, org chart, hierarchy, taxonomy, breakdown, structure)_

**When:** Parent/child: org charts, taxonomies, the decomposition of a goal into parts.
**Avoid:** Ordered steps or decisions with branches (use tls.g.flow).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`root\` | yes | object (label, sub, children) | Nested {label, sub?, children?: [{label, sub?, children?: [{label, sub?}]}]}. Max 3 levels, 15 nodes in all, 6 children per node. Labels 1-3 words. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: TB \\\\| LR | TB = top-down, LR = left to right (fits more leaves). |
| \`nodeStyle\` | no | enum: card \\\\| pill \\\\| avatar | avatar adds a round monogram (initials) to each card. |
| \`compact\` | no | boolean | Labels only, tighter boxes: fits more nodes. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_tree\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.g.tree\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"root\\": {
      \\"label\\": \\"Goal\\",
      \\"children\\": [
        {
          \\"label\\": \\"Grow revenue\\",
          \\"children\\": [
            {
              \\"label\\": \\"New markets\\"
            },
            {
              \\"label\\": \\"Upsell\\"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          \\"label\\": \\"Cut cost\\",
          \\"children\\": [
            {
              \\"label\\": \\"Automate\\"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.card\` — Card

Filled container with configurable padding. _(family: layout; keywords: card, container, padding, filled)_

**When:** Use to group children inside a visible, padded container.
**Avoid:** Do not use for transparent grouping (use tls.l.stack without style) or for a titled area with a divider (use tls.l.section).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`padding\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Inner padding of the card. |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) | Child blocks laid out inside the card. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_card\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.card\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"padding\\": \\"md\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.field\` — Field

Full-bleed background fill. _(family: layout; keywords: field, background, fill, full-bleed)_

**When:** Use as a solid-color background layer behind other content in an overlay.
**Avoid:** Do not use for visible content (it only paints a fill), or for a framed panel around content (use tls.l.card).

_No slots._

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_field\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.field\\",
  \\"props\\": {}
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.footer\` — Footer

Content + footer layout with configurable footer height. _(family: layout; keywords: footer, bottom, content, page)_

**When:** Use to add a persistent footer strip below the main content area.
**Avoid:** Do not use for an inline caption under one chart or image (use tls.t.caption).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`footerHeight\` | no | number (min 40, max 400) | Height of the footer area in slide units. |
| \`gutter\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Spacing between main content and footer. |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) (0–2 blocks) | First child is main content, second is the footer. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_footer\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.footer\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"footerHeight\\": 120,
    \\"gutter\\": \\"md\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.grid\` — Grid

Grid layout with configurable columns, rows, and gap. _(family: layout; keywords: grid, columns, rows, table)_

**When:** Use to arrange child blocks in a rows × columns grid.
**Avoid:** Do not use for a simple two-column layout (use tls.l.split) or for one line of items (use tls.l.row).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`columns\` | no | number (min 1, max 12) | Number of grid columns. |
| \`rows\` | no | number (min 1, max 12) | Number of grid rows. |
| \`gap\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Spacing between grid cells. |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) | Child blocks arranged in grid cells (row-major order). |
| \`sizing\` | no | enum: equal \\\\| content | How to distribute space among cells: equal (same size) or content (sized to intrinsic). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_grid\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.grid\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"columns\\": 2,
    \\"rows\\": 2,
    \\"gap\\": \\"md\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.grid-guide\` — Grid Guide

Alignment grid guide with configurable divisions. Editor-only: invisible in exported output. _(family: layout; keywords: grid, guide, alignment, editor)_

**When:** Use in the editor to show alignment guides for precise positioning.
**Avoid:** Do not use to lay out content: it only draws guides in the editor (use tls.l.grid for real columns).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`divisions\` | no | number (min 2, max 12) | Number of grid divisions on each axis. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_gguide\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.grid-guide\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"divisions\\": 3
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.overlay\` — Overlay

Layered children z-stacked in the same box. _(family: layout; keywords: overlay, layer, stack, z-index)_

**When:** Use to layer children on top of each other (backgrounds, watermarks).
**Avoid:** Do not use for sequential layout (use tls.l.stack or tls.l.row) or for a plain background fill (use tls.l.field).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) | Child blocks layered z-stack style (last child on top). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_overlay\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.overlay\\",
  \\"props\\": {},
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.repeater\` — Repeater

Repeats a template child for each item in a given direction. _(family: layout; keywords: repeater, repeat, loop, list)_

**When:** Use to lay out the same template block N times in a row or column.
**Avoid:** Do not use when the children differ from each other (use tls.l.stack or tls.l.grid).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`count\` | no | number (min 1, max 20) | Number of repetitions. |
| \`direction\` | no | enum: x \\\\| y | Lay out repetitions horizontally (x) or vertically (y). |
| \`gap\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Spacing between repeated items. |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) (0–1 blocks) | Template child to repeat. First child only — it is rendered count times. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_rep\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.repeater\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"count\\": 3,
    \\"direction\\": \\"y\\",
    \\"gap\\": \\"sm\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.row\` — Row

Horizontal row with gap. _(family: layout; keywords: row, horizontal, inline, gap)_

