### \`tls.l.split\` — Split

Two-panel split with configurable ratio and gutter. _(family: layout; keywords: split, columns, two-panel, sidebar)_

**When:** Use to divide a region into two panels (left/right or top/bottom).
**Avoid:** Do not use for three or more panels (use tls.l.grid) or for a narrow fixed-width side column (use tls.l.sidebar).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`ratio\` | no | number (min 0.1, max 0.9) | Fraction of space given to the first panel (0.1–0.9). |
| \`gutter\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Spacing between panels. |
| \`axis\` | no | enum: x \\\\| y | Split direction: x (left/right) or y (top/bottom). |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) (0–2 blocks) | Two child blocks, one per panel. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_split\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.split\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"ratio\\": 0.5,
    \\"gutter\\": \\"md\\",
    \\"axis\\": \\"x\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.l.stack\` — Stack

Vertical stack with gap. _(family: layout; keywords: stack, vertical, column, gap)_

**When:** Use to arrange child blocks vertically, one above the other.
**Avoid:** Do not use for horizontal arrangement (use tls.l.row) or for a grid of equal cells (use tls.l.grid).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`gap\` | no | enum: 3xs \\\\| 2xs \\\\| xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg \\\\| xl \\\\| 2xl \\\\| 3xl \\\\| 4xl | Spacing between stacked children. |
| \`children\` | no | blocks (allow: layout, text, data, diagram, composite, media) | Child blocks stacked vertically. |
| \`sizing\` | no | enum: equal \\\\| content | How to distribute space among children: equal (same size) or content (sized to intrinsic). |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_stack\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.l.stack\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"gap\\": \\"md\\"
  },
  \\"children\\": []
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.m.icon\` — Icon

SVG icon from the icon set, with optional color role. _(family: media; keywords: icon, symbol, graphic, svg)_

**When:** Use to display a named SVG icon (zap, shield, globe, check, etc.) with proper theming. Ideal for feature grids, labels, and decorative elements.
**Avoid:** Do not use for photographs (use tls.m.image) or for an icon that needs a text label (use tls.m.icon-label).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`icon\` | yes | icon | Choose a name from the icon list in the capability index. Unknown names render a placeholder. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Color role for the icon. Default uses accent color. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_icon_1\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.m.icon\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"icon\\": \\"zap\\",
    \\"color\\": \\"accent\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.m.icon-label\` — Icon Label

Icon with text label beneath. _(family: media; keywords: icon, label, button, nav, link)_

**When:** Use to label a feature, action, or section with an icon and brief text.
**Avoid:** Do not use for long descriptions (use tls.t.body) or for a grid of icon + title + description cells (use tls.c.feature-grid).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`icon\` | yes | icon | Choose from the icon set: zap, shield, globe, check, etc. |
| \`label\` | yes | text (max 100 chars) | Keep to 1-3 words. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default color role. |
| \`size\` | no | enum: sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg | Size of the icon+label group. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_il_1\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.m.icon-label\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"icon\\": \\"zap\\",
    \\"label\\": \\"Power\\",
    \\"color\\": \\"accent\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.m.icon-list\` — Icon list

Stacked points, each with its own icon, title and short description. _(family: media; keywords: icons, benefits, features, list, points)_

**When:** 3–6 benefits or features where each needs a recognisable icon, stacked in a column.
**Avoid:** A grid of features (use tls.c.feature-grid); points without icons (use tls.t.bullets).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (icon, title, text) (2–6 items) | Title 2–5 words; description one short sentence. Pick an icon that names the idea. |
| \`iconStyle\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| circle \\\\| square | circle and square put the icon on a tinted shape. |
| \`iconTone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| accent2 \\\\| text |  |
| \`spacing\` | no | enum: default \\\\| compact \\\\| roomy |  |
| \`showText\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_iconlist\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.m.icon-list\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"rocket\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Fast start\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Live in a week.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"shield\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Secure\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Audit trails included.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"icon\\": \\"sparkles\\",
        \\"title\\": \\"Polished\\",
        \\"text\\": \\"Looks right out of the box.\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"iconStyle\\": \\"circle\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.m.image\` — Image

Image with cover/contain fit, focal point, and optional caption. _(family: media; keywords: image, photo, picture, media, visual)_

**When:** Use to display a photograph, screenshot, or illustration with optional caption.
**Avoid:** Do not use for charts (use tls.d.bar), for background fills (use tls.l.field) or for an image with a text cluster (use tls.c.image-text).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`src\` | yes | image | Asset id or URL of the image to display. |
| \`alt\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | 1–10 words describing what the image shows. |
| \`fit\` | no | enum: cover \\\\| contain | How the image fills its box: cover (crop to fill) or contain (letterbox). |
| \`focal\` | no | object (fx, fy) | Focus area when fit is \\"cover\\". Default is center [0.5, 0.5]. |
| \`caption\` | no | text (max 200 chars) | Optional caption displayed below the image. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_image\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.m.image\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"src\\": \\"asset-hero-photo\\",
    \\"alt\\": \\"Team meeting in conference room\\",
    \\"fit\\": \\"cover\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"Team offsite, Q3 2026\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.body\` — Body

Paragraph body text with RichText, autofit, and multi-column. _(family: text; keywords: body, paragraph, text, prose, copy, description)_

**When:** Use for 1–3 sentences of body copy, descriptions, or prose.
**Avoid:** Do not use for bullet lists (use tls.t.bullets) or for small source lines under a chart (use tls.t.caption).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A concise paragraph, 1–3 sentences. Use bold for key terms. |
| \`columns\` | no | number (min 1, max 4) | Number of text columns. 1 = single paragraph. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`autoFit\` | no | boolean | Shrink font when content overflows the box. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_body\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.body\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Design systems scale because every \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"decision\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\" is made once.\\"
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"columns\\": 1,
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.bullets\` — Bullet list

Bullet list with dot/dash/chevron/number markers and indent levels. _(family: text; keywords: bullets, list, items, points, markers, unordered)_

**When:** Use for 2–8 short items that the audience should scan, not read.
**Avoid:** Do not use for sentences of prose (use tls.t.body), for ordered process steps (use tls.c.steps) or for icon-led feature cells (use tls.c.feature-grid). More than 8 items means two slides.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (text, level) (1–40 items) | 2–8 items, each 2–8 words. Start each with a verb or noun, not a full sentence. |
| \`marker\` | no | enum: dot \\\\| dash \\\\| chevron \\\\| number \\\\| icon | Bullet style. |
| \`indentLevels\` | no | boolean | Enable per-item indent levels for nested lists. |
| \`spacing\` | no | enum: xs \\\\| sm \\\\| md \\\\| lg | Vertical spacing between items. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_bullets\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.bullets\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Revenue up 42% YoY\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Enterprise APAC drove growth\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Churn fell to 3.1%\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"marker\\": \\"dot\\",
    \\"spacing\\": \\"sm\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.callout\` — Callout

Boxed note in one of five variants, with icon and optional title. _(family: text; keywords: callout, note, warning, tip, alert, caveat)_

**When:** Warnings, tips, notes and caveats beside the main content.
**Avoid:** The slide main conclusion (use tls.t.takeaway or tls.t.statement).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`title\` | no | text (max 50 chars) | 1–4 words, e.g. \\"Heads up\\". |
| \`text\` | yes | richText (max 240 chars) | One or two sentences. **Bold** works. |
| \`variant\` | no | enum: info \\\\| tip \\\\| warning \\\\| danger \\\\| success | Sets the colour role and default icon. |
| \`fill\` | no | enum: tint \\\\| outline \\\\| solid |  |
| \`icon\` | no | icon | Overrides the variant icon. |
| \`showIcon\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showTitle\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_callout\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.callout\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"title\\": \\"Tip\\",
    \\"text\\": \\"Run the demo on **battery** first, then plug in.\\",
    \\"variant\\": \\"tip\\",
    \\"fill\\": \\"tint\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.caption\` — Caption

Small caption text for images, charts, and media. _(family: text; keywords: caption, subtitle, description, label, small-text, source)_

**When:** Use to label a chart, image, or data source — 5–15 words maximum.
**Avoid:** Do not use for body text (use tls.t.body) or as a title (use tls.t.title or tls.t.subtitle).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | text (max 200 chars) | A brief description, 5–15 words. State what the reader should notice. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`position\` | no | enum: below \\\\| above \\\\| overlay | Where the caption sits relative to its referenced content. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_cap\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.caption\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"Source: internal Q3 financials\\",
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.checklist\` — Checklist

Checklist with a done, open or blocked state per item. _(family: text; keywords: checklist, todo, requirements, status, objectives)_

**When:** Requirements, prerequisites, launch checklists, learning objectives with a done state.
**Avoid:** Plain points without a state (use tls.t.bullets); support across options (use tls.d.compare-table).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (text, state) (2–10 items) | Short imperative or noun phrases. Set state on each; open is the default. |
| \`doneStyle\` | no | enum: check \\\\| strike \\\\| dim | strike crosses out done items, dim greys them. |
| \`spacing\` | no | enum: default \\\\| compact \\\\| roomy |  |
| \`columns\` | no | enum: 1 \\\\| 2 |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_checklist\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.checklist\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Draft the outline\\",
        \\"state\\": \\"done\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Review with the team\\",
        \\"state\\": \\"open\\"
      },
      {
        \\"text\\": \\"Legal approval\\",
        \\"state\\": \\"blocked\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"doneStyle\\": \\"strike\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.definition\` — Definition

A term with its definition, optional pronunciation, part of speech and example. _(family: text; keywords: definition, term, glossary, vocabulary, concept)_

**When:** Introducing a concept, glossary terms, vocabulary (lectures).
**Avoid:** Several term and value pairs (use tls.t.kv-list).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`term\` | yes | text (max 40 chars) | The word or phrase being defined, 1–3 words. |
| \`pronunciation\` | no | text (max 40 chars) | Optional, e.g. \\"/hyoo-RIS-tik/\\". |
| \`partOfSpeech\` | no | text (max 20 chars) | Optional, e.g. \\"noun\\". |
| \`definition\` | yes | richText (max 260 chars) | One or two sentences. **Bold** works. |
| \`example\` | no | text (max 160 chars) | Optional usage example. |
| \`layout\` | no | enum: stacked \\\\| inline | inline puts the term beside the definition. |
| \`termTone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| text |  |
| \`showPronunciation\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showExample\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_definition\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.definition\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"term\\": \\"Latency\\",
    \\"pronunciation\\": \\"/LAY-ten-see/\\",
    \\"partOfSpeech\\": \\"noun\\",
    \\"definition\\": \\"The **delay** between a request and the first byte of its response.\\",
    \\"example\\": \\"A 40 ms round trip feels instant.\\",
    \\"layout\\": \\"stacked\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.footnote\` — Footnote

Small-print source or footnote lines with an optional marker. _(family: text; keywords: footnote, source, reference, citation, small print)_

**When:** Citing data sources under a chart or table, and footnotes.
**Avoid:** A caption that describes an image (use tls.t.caption).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of text (max 200 chars) (1–4 items) | One source or note per line; no marker characters, the marker option adds them. |
| \`marker\` | no | enum: none \\\\| number \\\\| asterisk \\\\| source | source prefixes the first line with \\"Source:\\". |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| end |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_footnote\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.footnote\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      \\"Eurostat, 2025\\"
    ],
    \\"marker\\": \\"source\\",
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.hero-number\` — Hero Number

Large KPI number with optional unit and caption. _(family: text; keywords: kpi, number, stat, metric, hero, display, count)_

**When:** Use for one standout metric ($4.2M, 67%) that anchors a KPI slide.
**Avoid:** Do not use for several metrics in a row (use tls.c.kpi-row), for a number with a change arrow or sparkline (use tls.c.kpi-tile), or when the number should fill the whole slide (use tls.c.big-stat).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`value\` | no | text | The headline number. Include formatting, e.g. \\"$4.2M\\", \\"67%\\", \\"1,234\\". |
| \`unit\` | no | text | Unit label, 1–4 words. e.g. \\"Annual Revenue\\", \\"Completion Rate\\". |
| \`caption\` | no | text | Short context, 1 line max. e.g. \\"FY2024 total\\", \\"vs. last quarter\\". |
| \`format\` | no | enum: plain \\\\| compact \\\\| percent \\\\| currency | Number format hint for the renderer. |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: default \\\\| accent \\\\| muted | Colour emphasis for the headline number. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kpi\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.hero-number\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"value\\": \\"$4.2M\\",
    \\"unit\\": \\"Annual Revenue\\",
    \\"caption\\": \\"FY2024 total\\",
    \\"format\\": \\"currency\\",
    \\"emphasis\\": \\"accent\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.kicker\` — Kicker

Small label above the title with case and tracking options. _(family: text; keywords: kicker, eyebrow, label, category, tag, section)_

**When:** Use as a small category or section label above the title.
**Avoid:** Do not use for the slide title itself (use tls.t.title) or for a sentence of explanation (use tls.t.subtitle).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | text (max 60 chars) | A short label: section name, category, or status. UPPERCASE by default. 1–4 words. |
| \`case\` | no | enum: uppercase \\\\| lowercase \\\\| capitalize \\\\| none | Text transformation. Defaults to uppercase. |
| \`tracking\` | no | enum: wide \\\\| normal \\\\| narrow | Letter spacing for the kicker text. |
| \`marker\` | no | boolean | Show a small accent dot before the text. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kicker\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.kicker\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"OVERVIEW\\",
    \\"case\\": \\"uppercase\\",
    \\"tracking\\": \\"wide\\",
    \\"marker\\": false
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.kv-list\` — Key-value list

Key and value pairs in aligned columns, with dotted or ruled leaders. _(family: text; keywords: specs, facts, key value, details, schedule, terms)_

**When:** Specs, facts, terms and conditions, a schedule of times.
**Avoid:** Multi-column data (use tls.d.table).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (key, value) (2–10 items) | Short labels as keys; keep values to a phrase or a number with its unit. |
| \`leader\` | no | enum: none \\\\| dots \\\\| rule | dots join key to value; rule draws a hairline under each row. |
| \`valueAlign\` | no | enum: end \\\\| start |  |
| \`keyTone\` | no | enum: muted \\\\| text |  |
| \`columns\` | no | enum: 1 \\\\| 2 |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_kv\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.kv-list\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"key\\": \\"Start\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"09:00\\"
      },
      {
        \\"key\\": \\"Break\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"10:30\\"
      },
      {
        \\"key\\": \\"Finish\\",
        \\"value\\": \\"12:00\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"leader\\": \\"rule\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.numbered\` — Numbered list

Numbered points in order, one or two columns. _(family: text; keywords: numbered, ordered, ranked, reasons)_

**When:** Ordered points where the order or the count matters: \\"3 reasons\\", \\"5 rules\\".
**Avoid:** Unordered points (use tls.t.bullets); process steps (use tls.g.steps).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of richText (max 180 chars) (2–8 items) | Short sentences. Wrap a key phrase in **double asterisks** to bold it. |
| \`markerStyle\` | no | enum: decimal \\\\| padded \\\\| roman \\\\| alpha \\\\| badge | badge puts the number in a filled circle. |
| \`start\` | no | number (min 1) |  |
| \`spacing\` | no | enum: default \\\\| compact \\\\| roomy |  |
| \`columns\` | no | enum: 1 \\\\| 2 | Two balanced columns. |
| \`markerTone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| text \\\\| muted |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_numbered\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.numbered\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      \\"Define the audience\\",
      \\"State the **one** message\\",
      \\"Prove it with data\\",
      \\"Ask for the decision\\"
    ],
    \\"markerStyle\\": \\"badge\\",
    \\"markerTone\\": \\"accent\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.qa\` — Q and A

Question and answer pairs with Q/A badges or numbers. _(family: text; keywords: faq, questions, answers, q&a, review, objections)_

**When:** FAQ slides, review questions in a lecture, objection handling.
**Avoid:** A multiple-choice question (use tls.c.quiz).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of object (q, a) (1–5 items) | Questions as the audience would ask them; answers one to two sentences. |
| \`marker\` | no | enum: qa \\\\| numbered \\\\| none | qa shows \\"Q\\" and \\"A\\" badges; numbered numbers the questions. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_qa\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.qa\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      {
        \\"q\\": \\"Is it free?\\",
        \\"a\\": \\"Yes, for individuals.\\"
      },
      {
        \\"q\\": \\"Can I export?\\",
        \\"a\\": \\"To **PDF** and PPTX.\\"
      }
    ],
    \\"marker\\": \\"qa\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.quote\` — Quote

Pull quote with decorative quotation glyph, attribution, and role. _(family: text; keywords: quote, blockquote, pull-quote, attribution, testimonial)_

**When:** Use to feature a direct quote with attribution from a named person.
**Avoid:** Do not use for anonymous insights (use tls.t.takeaway) or for a customer quote with name, role and avatar (use tls.c.testimonial).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | no | richText | The quoted text. Can be 1–3 sentences. |
| \`attribution\` | no | text | Name of the person being quoted. |
| \`role\` | no | text | Title or role of the attributed person. |
| \`markStyle\` | no | enum: glyph \\\\| rule \\\\| none | How the quotation mark is rendered. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_quote\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.quote\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"The only way to do great work is to love what you do.\\",
    \\"attribution\\": \\"Steve Jobs\\",
    \\"role\\": \\"Co-founder, Apple\\",
    \\"markStyle\\": \\"glyph\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.statement\` — Statement

One large claim that fills the slide, key words emphasised. _(family: text; keywords: statement, claim, conclusion, message, big text)_

**When:** A single claim or conclusion that should fill the slide's attention.
**Avoid:** A quotation from a person (use tls.t.quote); a takeaway beside other content (use tls.t.takeaway).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText (max 140 chars) | One claim, a single sentence. Wrap the 1–3 key words in **double asterisks**. |
| \`attribution\` | no | text (max 60 chars) | Optional source line, e.g. \\"Q3 board review\\". |
| \`size\` | no | enum: xl \\\\| lg \\\\| md | Shrinks to fit, never below md. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center |  |
| \`emphasis\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| underline \\\\| highlight | How the **bold** words render: accent colour, accent underline, or accent highlight. |
| \`showAttribution\` | no | boolean |  |
| \`showMark\` | no | boolean |  |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_statement\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.statement\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"Retention, not acquisition, is our **growth engine**.\\",
    \\"attribution\\": \\"FY26 strategy\\",
    \\"size\\": \\"lg\\",
    \\"emphasis\\": \\"highlight\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.subtitle\` — Subtitle

Secondary heading below the title with RichText support. _(family: text; keywords: subtitle, subheading, secondary)_

**When:** Use to add context, date, or audience below the title.
**Avoid:** Do not use for long paragraphs (use tls.t.body) or as the slide title itself (use tls.t.title).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A brief supporting sentence or phrase. 3–12 words. Never repeat the title. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_sub\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.subtitle\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Q3 FY2026 · prepared for the \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"board\\",
          \\"italic\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.tags\` — Tags

Wrapping row of pill-shaped tags in soft, outline or solid tone. _(family: text; keywords: tags, chips, pills, skills, keywords, labels)_

**When:** Skills, technologies, keywords, categories, labels on a profile.
**Avoid:** Sentences (use tls.t.bullets); a single eyebrow label (use tls.t.kicker).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`items\` | yes | list of text (max 30 chars) (1–12 items) | Single words or short noun phrases, 1–3 words each. |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: soft \\\\| outline \\\\| solid |  |
| \`shape\` | no | enum: pill \\\\| rect |  |
| \`size\` | no | enum: md \\\\| sm \\\\| lg |  |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center |  |
| \`colorBy\` | no | enum: single \\\\| cycle | cycle walks the series colours. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_tags\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.tags\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"items\\": [
      \\"Python\\",
      \\"SQL\\",
      \\"Statistics\\",
      \\"Dashboards\\"
    ],
    \\"tone\\": \\"soft\\",
    \\"colorBy\\": \\"cycle\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.takeaway\` — Takeaway

Highlighted insight text with accent bar and optional label. _(family: text; keywords: takeaway, insight, callout, highlight, key-point)_

**When:** Use to call out a key insight, conclusion, or \\"so what\\" from data.
**Avoid:** Do not use for quotes from named people (use tls.t.quote) or for ordinary body text (use tls.t.body).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | no | richText | The insight or takeaway. 1–2 sentences, direct and clear. |
| \`tone\` | no | enum: accent \\\\| positive \\\\| warning \\\\| muted | Visual tone that controls the accent bar and surface tint. |
| \`icon\` | no | icon | Optional icon shown beside the label. |
| \`label\` | no | text | Short label, 1–3 words. e.g. \\"Key Insight\\", \\"Remember\\". |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_take\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.takeaway\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": \\"Compute spend grew 2.4x while revenue grew 1.2x.\\",
    \\"tone\\": \\"accent\\",
    \\"label\\": \\"Key Insight\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.t.title\` — Title

Slide title with inline styling, autofit, and truncation. _(family: text; keywords: title, heading, hero, headline, slide)_

**When:** Use as the primary heading on every content slide — the single most important text.
**Avoid:** Do not use for an opening slide (use tls.c.hero), for a secondary line (use tls.t.subtitle) or for a small label above a title (use tls.t.kicker).

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`text\` | yes | richText | A concise slide title. Bold one key word for emphasis. Never a full sentence. |
| \`size\` | no | enum: display \\\\| title \\\\| heading \\\\| subheading | Type scale step for the title. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |
| \`rule\` | no | boolean | Show a short accent rule below the title. |
| \`maxLines\` | no | number (min 1, max 10) | Maximum number of lines before truncation. Truncation adds a visible marker. |
| \`color\` | no | color (role or theme token — never hex) | Override the default text color role. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_title\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.title\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"text\\": {
      \\"runs\\": [
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"Revenue \\"
        },
        {
          \\"text\\": \\"grew 42%\\",
          \\"bold\\": true
        }
      ]
    },
    \\"size\\": \\"title\\",
    \\"align\\": \\"start\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### \`tls.x.page-number\` — Page Number

Page number chrome element for slide footers. _(family: chrome; keywords: page, number, footer, pagination)_

**When:** Use to indicate the current page position in a multi-slide document.
**Avoid:** Do not use as a content block: it is slide furniture only.

| Slot | Required | Type | Guidance |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`number\` | yes | number (min 1) | Typically 1-2 digits. |
| \`align\` | no | enum: start \\\\| center \\\\| end | Text alignment. |

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"b_page_1\\",
  \\"type\\": \\"tls.x.page-number\\",
  \\"props\\": {
    \\"number\\": 1,
    \\"align\\": \\"center\\"
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Worked example — a valid slide

Zero coordinates, zero colour values, zero font sizes. Region names come from the layout (\`two-column\` → \`title\`, \`left\`, \`right\`); block types and slots come from the tables above.

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"id\\": \\"sl_03\\",
  \\"layout\\": \\"two-column\\",
  \\"role\\": \\"content\\",
  \\"rhythm\\": \\"dense\\",
  \\"regions\\": {
    \\"title\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b1\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.title\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": {
            \\"runs\\": [
              {
                \\"text\\": \\"Margin fell on \\"
              },
              {
                \\"text\\": \\"infrastructure\\",
                \\"bold\\": true
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    ],
    \\"left\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b2\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.d.bar\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"categories\\": [
            \\"Q1\\",
            \\"Q2\\",
            \\"Q3\\"
          ],
          \\"series\\": [
            64,
            64,
            61
          ],
          \\"highlightIndex\\": 2
        },
        \\"motion\\": {
          \\"preset\\": \\"bars-grow\\",
          \\"order\\": 2,
          \\"trigger\\": \\"onClick\\"
        }
      }
    ],
    \\"right\\": [
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b3\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.takeaway\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": \\"Compute spend grew 2.4× while revenue grew 1.2×.\\"
        },
        \\"motion\\": {
          \\"preset\\": \\"fade-up\\",
          \\"order\\": 3
        }
      },
      {
        \\"id\\": \\"b4\\",
        \\"type\\": \\"tls.t.caption\\",
        \\"props\\": {
          \\"text\\": \\"Source: internal Q3 financials\\"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  \\"notes\\": \\"Land on the 61 — this is the hinge slide.\\"
}
\`\`\`
"
`;

